@*
    FundCircuit — the fund, drawn as the thing it is.

    Capital leaves an investor, becomes panels on a household's roof, and comes
    back as instalments that pay the investor's interest. That is a circuit, and
    the company's seal already has circuit routing running across its shield —
    so rather than illustrate the scheme with a photograph of a roof, the landing
    page draws it as a board, with the seal soldered on at the junction.

    It follows the same rules CircuitField does, because they are what make a
    drawing read as a board instead of as clip art: segments on 90° and 45°
    only, and every run ending in a via. The two runs enter the seal side by
    side, twenty units apart, the way a paired signal is routed.

    Colour carries direction, and the tokens already say which is which. Gold is
    the brand's — so gold is the capital going out. Cyan is instrumentation — so
    cyan is what is measured coming back. The chevrons say the same thing again
    without colour.

    This is the page's one orchestrated moment. The whole board is visible from
    the first frame, unlit; then light travels out along the gold run and home
    along the cyan one, once, in the order the money actually moves. Nothing
    loops, and base.css removes it entirely under prefers-reduced-motion. Every
    --at below is a start time on that one clock.

    Two routings of the same board, because a wide one cannot be squeezed onto a
    phone: its labels are SVG text and scale with the drawing, and below about
    960px they would drop under 12px. CSS shows exactly one, and display:none
    takes the other out of the accessibility tree along with it.

    The labels in capitals are the board's silkscreen — component names printed
    on the substrate, set like the lettering round the seal's ring. They are the
    only capitals on the page besides the wordmark.
*@

<div class="circuit">
    <svg class="circuit__board circuit__board--wide"
         viewBox="0 0 1120 310"
         role="img"
         aria-label="@Summary"
         focusable="false">

        <g class="circuit__base">
            <path d="M24 70H300L380 150H740L820 70H1096" />
            <path d="M1096 250H820L740 170H380L300 250H24" />
            <circle cx="24" cy="70" r="8" />
            <circle cx="1096" cy="70" r="8" />
            <circle cx="1096" cy="250" r="8" />
            <circle cx="24" cy="250" r="8" />
        </g>

        <path class="circuit__run circuit__run--out" pathLength="1"
              d="M24 70H300L380 150H740L820 70H1096" />
        <path class="circuit__run circuit__run--back" pathLength="1"
              d="M1096 250H820L740 170H380L300 250H24" />

        @* Out: investor to household, left to right. *@
        <circle class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--out" style="--at: 400ms" cx="24" cy="70" r="8" />
        <path class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--out" style="--at: 700ms"
              transform="translate(176 70)" d="M-6 -7 2 0-6 7" />
        <path class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--out" style="--at: 1500ms"
              transform="translate(952 70)" d="M-6 -7 2 0-6 7" />
        <circle class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--out" style="--at: 1750ms" cx="1096" cy="70" r="8" />

        @* Back: household to investor, right to left. *@
        <circle class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--back" style="--at: 1900ms" cx="1096" cy="250" r="8" />
        <path class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--back" style="--at: 2200ms"
              transform="translate(944 250)" d="M6 -7-2 0 6 7" />
        <path class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--back" style="--at: 3000ms"
              transform="translate(168 250)" d="M6 -7-2 0 6 7" />
        <circle class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--back" style="--at: 3250ms" cx="24" cy="250" r="8" />

        @* The disc is what makes the runs pass *under* the badge rather than
           through it: the artwork's corners are transparent, and without a
           ground of its own the traces would show in them. It is a few units
           smaller than the badge on purpose. Any wider and it shows as a dark
           collar with the runs stopping short of it, which reads as four loose
           ends rather than as one board. *@
        <circle class="circuit__seat" cx="560" cy="160" r="64" />
        <image class="circuit__seal" href="img/jte-seal.png"
               x="490" y="88.4" width="140" height="143.1" />

        <text class="circuit__label" x="44" y="46">Capital placed</text>
        <text class="circuit__label" x="1076" y="46" text-anchor="end">Solar fitted now</text>
        <text class="circuit__label" x="1076" y="290" text-anchor="end">Instalments on agreed terms</text>
        <text class="circuit__label" x="44" y="290">Fixed interest, and a system of their own</text>

        <text class="circuit__silk" x="24" y="165">Investor</text>
        <text class="circuit__silk" x="1096" y="165" text-anchor="end">Household</text>
        <text class="circuit__silk" x="560" y="274" text-anchor="middle">The fund</text>
    </svg>

    <svg class="circuit__board circuit__board--tall"
         viewBox="0 0 360 620"
         role="img"
         aria-label="@Summary"
         focusable="false">

        <g class="circuit__base">
            <path d="M36 56V136L170 270V350L36 484V564" />
            <path d="M324 564V484L190 350V270L324 136V56" />
            <circle cx="36" cy="56" r="8" />
            <circle cx="36" cy="564" r="8" />
            <circle cx="324" cy="564" r="8" />
            <circle cx="324" cy="56" r="8" />
        </g>

        <path class="circuit__run circuit__run--out" pathLength="1"
              d="M36 56V136L170 270V350L36 484V564" />
        <path class="circuit__run circuit__run--back" pathLength="1"
              d="M324 564V484L190 350V270L324 136V56" />

        @* Out: investor to household, down the left. *@
        <circle class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--out" style="--at: 400ms" cx="36" cy="56" r="8" />
        <path class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--out" style="--at: 650ms"
              transform="translate(36 104)" d="M-7 -6 0 2 7 -6" />
        <path class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--out" style="--at: 1550ms"
              transform="translate(36 528)" d="M-7 -6 0 2 7 -6" />
        <circle class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--out" style="--at: 1750ms" cx="36" cy="564" r="8" />

        @* Back: household to investor, up the right. *@
        <circle class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--back" style="--at: 1900ms" cx="324" cy="564" r="8" />
        <path class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--back" style="--at: 2150ms"
              transform="translate(324 516)" d="M-7 6 0 -2 7 6" />
        <path class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--back" style="--at: 3050ms"
              transform="translate(324 92)" d="M-7 6 0 -2 7 6" />
        <circle class="circuit__mark circuit__mark--back" style="--at: 3250ms" cx="324" cy="56" r="8" />

        <circle class="circuit__seat" cx="180" cy="310" r="57" />
        <image class="circuit__seal" href="img/jte-seal.png"
               x="118" y="246.6" width="124" height="126.8" />

        <text class="circuit__label" x="56" y="88">
            <tspan x="56">Capital</tspan>
            <tspan x="56" dy="21">placed</tspan>
        </text>
        <text class="circuit__label" x="304" y="80" text-anchor="end">
            <tspan x="304">Fixed interest,</tspan>
            <tspan x="304" dy="21">and a system</tspan>
            <tspan x="304" dy="21">of their own</tspan>
        </text>
        <text class="circuit__label" x="56" y="520">
            <tspan x="56">Solar fitted</tspan>
            <tspan x="56" dy="21">now</tspan>
        </text>
        <text class="circuit__label" x="304" y="500" text-anchor="end">
            <tspan x="304">Instalments</tspan>
            <tspan x="304" dy="21">on agreed</tspan>
            <tspan x="304" dy="21">terms</tspan>
        </text>

        <text class="circuit__silk" x="180" y="30" text-anchor="middle">Investor</text>
        <text class="circuit__silk" x="180" y="604" text-anchor="middle">Household</text>
        <text class="circuit__silk" x="180" y="408" text-anchor="middle">The fund</text>
    </svg>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The drawing in one sentence, for anyone who cannot see it. It names the
    /// four movements in the order the light travels them.
    /// </summary>
    private const string Summary =
        "How the fund circulates. An investor places capital with the fund. "
        + "The fund fits solar on a household's roof. "
        + "The household pays fixed monthly instalments on agreed terms. "
        + "Those payments return to the investor as a fixed interest, "
        + "along with a solar system of their own.";
}
